      "heading": "B — Audience, level and prerequisites: alcohol and drug impairment, DWI limits, implied consent, penalties and cannabis rules",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, level and prerequisites: alcohol and drug impairment, DWI limits, implied consent, penalties and cannabis rules\nAudience: first-time Minnesota Class D applicants, especially drivers under twenty-one, who face the no-tolerance rule.\nWhy it matters to a first-timer: the impairment basics [A01], the DWI limits and implied consent duties [A03] and the underage rule and interlock limit [A05] are among the most frequently tested items in the manual.\nLevel: moderate to high; many look-alike decimals (point zero two, point zero four, point zero eight, point one six) and penalty periods by offense.\nPrerequisites: the license withdrawal chapter on suspension, revocation and cancellation.\n",
